<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2512" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Andes</span></b> , ium, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Andecāvi</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Andicāvi</span></b> , ōrum,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				Gallic tribe in the region of the present Anjou</i>, with a
			town of the same name, now <i>Angors;</i> form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Andes</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G.
				2, 35</span></i>.—Form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Andecāvi</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 3,
			41</span></i>.—Form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Andi-cāvi</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 18,
				32, § 107</span></i> Jan; cf. Mann. Gall. 163.</div>
